<title>USA: Magnum to buy oil, gas properties for $144 million.</title>
<headline>Magnum to buy oil, gas properties for $144 million.</headline>
<dateline>IRVING, Texas 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Magnum Petroleum Inc. said Friday it has agreed to buy oil and gas properties from subsidiaries of Burlington Resources Inc. for about $144 million.</p>
<p>The properties in west Texas and southeast New Mexico would boost annual revenues to more than $50 million and total assets to about $250 million, Magnum said.</p>
<p>Magnum said it expects the deal to close by April 30. The purchase will be funded with bank loans and privately sold securities.</p>
<p>Irving, Texas-based Magnum stock fell 12.5 cents to $6.50 in afternoon trading on the American Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
